# Review gate

After finishing an implementation or test slice:

1. Review the diff against challenge requirements and architecture rules.
2. List concrete findings (bugs, a11y gaps, perf smells, design drift).
3. Fix clear issues found in that slice.
4. Re-run relevant checks (`npm run typecheck`, `npm test`, and/or E2E smokes).
5. Only then mark the corresponding `docs/todo.md` checkboxes and move on.

Do not skip the gate to “save time” — regressions caught early are the point.
